{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615097-the-blood-will-tell","id":615097,"title":"The blood will tell","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-04T08:14:51-07:00","id":615097,"title":"The blood will tell","content":"So, several years ago I had a newly-awakened ancient Mekhet grab an ancilla and begin drinking. As she drank, she learned much of the ancilla\u2019s history, personality, and intentions. Knowing all this allowed her to trust and, to some extent, manipulate the PC. I didn\u2019t write it up, I just decided she could do that. <br /> <br /> The thread on disciplines above 5 got me thinking about how to characterize this particular ability. Is it Auspex 4, with bonus dice based on the number of Vitae taken? Is it a Devotion with prerequisites of Auspex 4 and a certain blood potency? How would you build this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:37:39-07:00","id":615277,"title":"","content":"It's a Bloodline ability. Mnemosyne from the Mekhet clan book had a Discipline that allowed them to steal memories from a victim by feeding on them. I'm guessing in 2e this would probably be handled as a Gift rather than a Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:03:07-07:00","id":615316,"title":"","content":"And if your friendly ancient Mekhet isn't a Mnemosyne, then fiat it away. Old vampires are scary and can do a lot of spooky things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:06:15-07:00","id":615319,"title":"","content":"Gifts are basically bloodline specific devotions, to be clear. Still unknown what bloodline disciplines might be like in 2e.<br /> <br /> I might house rule a blood potency requirement for a devotion, but not &quot;officially&quot; put that in there because then I have to decide what happens when blood potency drops. I agree with Auspex 4 as a prerequisite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:26:40-07:00","id":615385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615097-the-blood-will-tell?p=615319#post615319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gifts are basically bloodline specific devotions, to be clear. Still unknown what bloodline disciplines might be like in 2e.<br /> <br /> I might house rule a blood potency requirement for a devotion, but not &amp;quot;officially&amp;quot; put that in there because then I have to decide what happens when blood potency drops. I agree with Auspex 4 as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodline Gifts aren't necessarily Devotions. Look at the Neglatu, their Gifts are just straight up changes to the template. Similarly, the Kerberoi get a template change as a Gift and a unique Merit that synergies with their Gift. Khaibit are the only official 2e bloodline so far that gets Devotions for a Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:54:12-07:00","id":615413,"title":"","content":"Auspex 2/3 can arguably do all this already. Why reinvent the wheel? At worst, a minor devotion would work as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:32:32-07:00","id":615458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615097-the-blood-will-tell?p=615413#post615413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex 2/3 can arguably do all this already. Why reinvent the wheel? At worst, a minor devotion would work as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely true. If you're looking for a dice bonus, I bet feeding from someone would probably count for that +3 &quot;Intimate&quot; connection.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:53:35-07:00","id":615480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615097-the-blood-will-tell?p=615385#post615385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodline Gifts aren't necessarily Devotions. Look at the Neglatu, their Gifts are just straight up changes to the template. Similarly, the Kerberoi get a template change as a Gift and a unique Merit that synergies with their Gift. Khaibit are the only official 2e bloodline so far that gets Devotions for a Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>All that is true, but I was speaking more in terms of devotion or discipline. I think being bloodline specific indicates they are atypical, but if you consider the view too simplistic. Gifts are <i>actually</i> gifts. That seems a bit obvious though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T16:22:21-07:00","id":615695,"title":"","content":"In the end, there are multiple possibilities for it. Including just Auspex 4 with scene flavor. If in doubt, or if you think of anything else more interesting that you want this power to do, just make it a Devotion.<br /> <br /> And probably not even one with BP requirement, just Auspex 4. Just because it is interesting and was developed by an elder, doesn't mean it is so powerful, specially because the elder just awakened from Torpor, so maybe it doesn't have the BP so high right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T19:22:49-07:00","id":617030,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions. Rereading Auspex 4, it is more encompassing than in the previous version. May amp it a bit with a Devotion, but it is likely sufficient for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T05:41:57-07:00","id":617637,"title":"","content":"I was thinking this knowledge transfer was happening pretty quickly. If time isn't a factor then Auspex 4 would be sufficient to do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T08:10:43-07:00","id":617779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615097-the-blood-will-tell?p=617637#post617637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking this knowledge transfer was happening pretty quickly. If time isn't a factor then Auspex 4 would be sufficient to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was another version this somewhere else as well. Ancient mysteries? Dance Macabre? I can't remember.<br /> Not sure if required auspex or not but I don't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}